{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{# render_mode guard MUST be within the first 5 lines (see 0330). #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{# Relationships - how to answer now, at the end of the prompt (wpm87-88;     #}
{# SkyrimNet's lead developer, 2026-11-03: "things at the very start and very #}
{# end get the most attention", and an instruction for handling the request  #}
{# "doesn't really belong in the character bio"). The bio (0330-0332) says    #}
{# who they are and how things stand; this says what to do in this reply:    #}
{# the planner's next question and marks, the Wedding and Marriage actions,  #}
{# the step of a wedding under way, and keeping the numbers unsaid. From     #}
{# 29.1 rc2 the action list sits in the cached system message, and these     #}
{# lines, mid-bio, lost to it: Senna settled six things in seven replies and #}
{# wrote no ACTION line for any.                                             #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if not is_player(npc.UUID) %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esl") or is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esp") %}
{% set snrom_rom = get_romance(npc.UUID) %}
{# THE NUMBERS UNSAID (from the end of 0330, wpm88). #}
{% if snrom_rom and default(snrom_rom.enrolled, false) %}

Do not state your tier, your points, or any number about your bond with {{ player.name }}. Do not announce the state of the relationship. Let it show in your manner, what you notice, what you assume you are allowed to say.
{% endif %}
{% if render_mode == "full" %}
{% set snrom_embed = default(embed_actions_in_dialogue, false) and exists("eligible_actions") %}
{% set snrom_wedding = false %}
{% set snrom_marriage = false %}
{% if snrom_embed %}{% for a in eligible_actions %}{% if a.name == "Wedding" %}{% set snrom_wedding = true %}{% elif a.name == "Marriage" %}{% set snrom_marriage = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{# ── The hired planner: the next question, and marks (from 0332, wpm88) ── #}
{% set snrom_planner = false %}
{% set snrom_wp = get_wedding_planner(npc.UUID) %}
{% if snrom_wp and default(snrom_wp.planner, 0) == 1 and existsIn(snrom_wp, "couples") %}
{% for c in snrom_wp.couples %}
{% if default(c.hired, 0) == 1 %}
{% set snrom_planner = true %}
{# STAND HERE IS A MARK (seen in play, wpm61): "Danica, I want you to stand
   here" chose no action, and "And then I will stand here" was not taken as
   wedding business at all. #}
{% if c.plan.place != "" %}

Whenever {{ player.name }} says someone will stand or gather here - "{% if c.plan.officiant != "" %}{{ c.plan.officiant }}{% else %}you{% endif %}, stand here", "I will stand here", "{{ c.betrothed }} will stand here", "{{ c.betrothed }}'s guests gather here", "my guests here" - that is a mark for {{ c.plan.place }}, one each time it is said, whoever it is for{% if c.plan.officiant != "" %} ({{ c.plan.officiant }} marries them{% if c.plan.officiant == c.plan.planner %}: that is you{% endif %}){% endif %}. A mark is made where {{ player.name }} stands as they say it: you cannot mark a spot for them, nor one they point at - ask them to go and stand on it.
{% endif %}
{# THE NEXT QUESTION, NAMED (seen in play, wpm55): told only to "ask about
   the next thing not yet settled", Danica, asked "anything else?", said
   "only bring the rings" and asked nothing. The one question, worded; what
   is still needed comes first. #}
{% set unsettled = default(c.plan.unsettled, []) %}
{% if length(c.plan.open) > 0 or length(unsettled) > 0 %}
{% if length(c.plan.open) > 0 %}{% set next = first(c.plan.open) %}{% else %}{% set next = first(unsettled) %}{% endif %}

Lead them through the wedding to {{ c.betrothed }}, as a planner does. When {{ player.name }} talks wedding business with you, or asks whether anything else is needed, settle what they bring and then ask them, in your own words, {% if next == "day" %}what day they want to be married{% elif next == "hour" %}at what hour of the day{% elif next == "place" %}where they want to be married - a place by name, or, if they are standing at it, right where they are{% elif next == "officiant" %}who they want to marry them{% elif next == "near" %}what {{ c.plan.place }} is by - the temple, hall, inn or town nearest it - since the guests cannot find their way there by that name alone{% elif next == "guests" %}who they will invite{% elif next == "sides" %}whose guest {{ first(c.plan.unsided) }} is - {{ c.betrothed }}'s or {{ player.name }}'s{% if length(c.plan.unsided) > 1 %} (they may answer for the others too: {% for g in c.plan.unsided %}{% if not loop.is_first %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}){% endif %}{% elif next == "layout" %}{% set um = default(c.plan.unmarked, []) %}where {% for m in um %}{% if m == "officiant" %}{% if c.plan.officiant != "" %}{{ c.plan.officiant }}{% else %}the one marrying them{% endif %} will stand{% elif m == "you" %}the two of them will stand{% elif m == "theirs" %}{{ c.betrothed }}'s guests will gather{% else %}{{ player.name }}'s guests will gather{% endif %}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} at {{ c.plan.place }}, which {{ player.name }} shows you by standing on each spot as they say so - or whether they would leave {% if length(default(c.plan.marked, [])) > 0 %}the rest{% else %}it{% endif %} to you{% elif next == "ceremony" %}whether they want the ceremony as it usually goes - {% if c.plan.officiant != "" %}{{ c.plan.officiant }}'s{% else %}the officiant's{% endif %} address to everyone gathered, a reading or blessing, the rings exchanged before they are pronounced married, and the kiss - or would leave any of it out{% elif next == "theirRing" %}the metal of {{ c.betrothed }}'s wedding ring: gold, silver or ebony{% elif next == "yourRing" %}the metal of {{ player.name }}'s wedding ring: gold, silver or ebony{% else %}what {{ c.betrothed }} will wear on the day{% endif %}. Do not tell them everything is ready while that is unanswered. One question at a time; a plain answer is an answer ("no guests", "the usual ceremony"): take it and go on to the next.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{# ── The Wedding action: the planner and the betrothed (wpm87) ── #}
{% if snrom_wedding and (snrom_planner or get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, "SNRom_Marriage") == 1) %}

The wedding plan changes only through the Wedding action. If this reply agrees to any part of it - the day, the place (a named place, or right where {{ player.name }} is standing), who marries them, who is invited and whose guests they are, where someone will stand, the ceremony, a wedding ring, the clothes - end it with `ACTION: Wedding PARAMS: {"intent": "..."}`, and say in the intent exactly what was agreed, with the names: "invite Orla and Senna as {{ player.name }}'s guests", "the wedding is right here; the officiant stands here". Saying it is noted, written down or marked does not record it.
{% endif %}
{# ── The Marriage action: a yes either way (from 0330, wpm87) ── #}
{% if snrom_marriage and snrom_rom and default(snrom_rom.marriage.canAccept, 0) == 1 %}

If in this reply you say yes to marrying {{ player.name }}, or {{ player.name }} says yes to you - even days after it was asked - end it with the Marriage action. Without it the promise is only words.
{% endif %}
{# ── A wedding under way: this step (from 0331 and 0330, wpm88) ──────────
   WHAT COMES NEXT, IN EVERY STEP (seen in play, wpm74): a reply to a line is
   written before that line moves the wedding on. Danica's reply to the
   player's "I do" was written while this still said "wait for their answer;
   do not ask Olfina yet" - and, told only what not to do, she pronounced them
   married. So each step that waits on someone says what your next words are
   once they have spoken. Steps (Ceremony.h): 1 open and ask for the player's
   vows, 2 the player's vows, 3 the betrothed's, 4 ask the player, 5 their
   answer, 6 ask the betrothed, 7 their answer, 8 pronounce; a planned
   wedding's 10 address, 11 reading, 12 rings invited, 14 rings given, 13 the
   kiss, 15 presented. 6 IS NOT YET THE BETROTHED'S TURN (wpm77). #}
{% set off = get_officiant(npc.UUID) %}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and default(off.ceremony, 0) > 0 %}
{% set them = default(off.marrying, "your betrothed") %}
{% set step = off.ceremony %}

{% if step == 10 %}
Now: everyone has gathered. Address them all, in your own words: why they are here, and who is being married. Do not ask for vows yet.
{% elif step == 11 %}
Now: give a short reading or blessing fitting the faith that is yours and the two of them. Do not ask for vows yet.
{% elif step == 12 %}
Now: both have said yes. Invite {{ player.name }} and {{ them }} to exchange rings, and stop there: let them do it. Not the pronouncement yet: that comes after the rings.
{% elif step == 14 %}
Now: you have invited them to exchange rings, and {{ them }} is putting a ring on {{ player.name }}'s finger. Watch, and say nothing yet. Once it is on, your next words pronounce them married{% if default(off.kiss, 0) == 1 %} and invite them to kiss{% endif %}.
{% elif step == 1 %}
Now: open the wedding with a few words fitting the moment, then ask {{ player.name }} to speak their vows to {{ them }}. Not "do you take" yet: that question comes only after both of them have spoken their vows.
{% elif step == 2 %}
Now: {{ player.name }} is speaking their vows to {{ them }}. Listen. When they have finished, it is {{ them }}'s turn to speak their vows: you may invite them to, but ask no other question yet.
{% elif step == 3 %}
Now: {{ them }} is speaking their vows to {{ player.name }}. Listen. When they have finished, your next words ask {{ player.name }}, plainly, whether they take {{ them }} to be their {% if default(off.marryingFemale, 0) == 1 %}wife{% else %}husband{% endif %}.
{% elif step == 4 %}
Now: both have spoken their vows. Ask {{ player.name }}, plainly, whether they take {{ them }} to be their {% if default(off.marryingFemale, 0) == 1 %}wife{% else %}husband{% endif %}.
{% elif step == 5 %}
Now: you have asked {{ player.name }} whether they take {{ them }}, and their answer comes next; do not answer for them. When they have said yes, your next words ask {{ them }} the same: whether they take {{ player.name }}. Not the pronouncement: {{ them }} has not been asked yet.
{% elif step == 6 %}
Now: {{ player.name }} has said yes. Ask {{ them }} whether they take {{ player.name }}. Ask it even if {{ them }} has already said something like yes: the question is yours to put, and their answer is to you. Do not pronounce them married until {{ them }} has answered you.
{% elif step == 7 %}
Now: you have asked {{ them }} whether they take {{ player.name }}, and their answer comes next; let them answer for themselves. When they have said yes, your next words {% if default(off.rings, 0) == 1 %}invite the two of them to exchange rings - the pronouncement comes after the rings{% else %}pronounce them married{% if default(off.kiss, 0) == 1 %} and invite them to kiss{% endif %}{% endif %}.
{% elif step == 13 %}
Now: you have pronounced them married and invited them to kiss. Let them; it is their moment, and you have nothing to say until it has passed. When it has, your next words present them to everyone gathered, married.
{% elif step == 15 %}
Now: {{ player.name }} and {{ them }} have kissed, married. Present them to everyone gathered, in your own words: a few warm, plain words that end the ceremony and invite everyone to greet them.
{% elif step == 8 %}
Now: both {{ player.name }} and {{ them }} have said yes. Pronounce them married, in your own words{% if default(off.kiss, 0) == 1 %}, and invite them to kiss{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
{% elif snrom_rom and default(snrom_rom.marriageOurs, 1) == 1 and existsIn(snrom_rom, "marriage") and default(snrom_rom.marriage.state, "none") == "engaged" and default(snrom_rom.marriage.ceremony, 0) > 0 %}
{% set wed = default(snrom_rom.marriage.ceremony, 0) %}
{% set wed_by = default(snrom_rom.marriage.ceremonyOfficiant, "the officiant") %}

{% if wed == 10 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} is addressing everyone gathered for your wedding. Listen; it is not your turn yet.
{% elif wed == 11 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} is giving a reading, or a blessing. Listen; it is not your turn yet.
{% elif wed == 12 %}
Now: you have both said yes, and {{ wed_by }} is about to invite the two of you to exchange rings. Wait for that; it is not your turn yet.
{% elif wed == 14 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} has invited the two of you to exchange rings. Put a ring on {{ player.name }}'s finger, as they put one on yours, with a word if you wish. Not the kiss yet: {{ wed_by }} has still to pronounce you married.
The rings are your wedding rings, chosen for today, and they go on as you speak: hand over nothing from your pack, and choose no action for it - no other ring is part of this.
{% elif wed == 13 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} has pronounced you married, and invites the two of you to kiss. Kiss {{ player.name }}, married to you now, as yourself, with a word if you wish. This is the first moment of your marriage.
{% elif wed == 15 %}
Now: you have kissed, married, and {{ wed_by }} is presenting the two of you to everyone gathered. Stand with {{ player.name }} and let them; you need say nothing.
{% elif wed <= 2 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} has opened, and it is {{ player.name }}'s turn to speak their vows to you. Listen; it is not your turn yet. When they have spoken them, your next words are your own vows to {{ player.name }}.
{% elif wed == 3 %}
Now: {{ player.name }} has spoken their vows. Speak your own vows to {{ player.name }}, in your own words. These are your vows, not yet an answer to any question.
{% elif wed <= 5 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} is asking {{ player.name }} whether they take you. Listen for their answer; it is not your turn yet. Whatever {{ player.name }} says now, even said to you, is their answer to {{ wed_by }}, not a question for you. Do not answer it for yourself: no "I do", no yes of your own, no vow. {{ wed_by }} will ask you next, and only then is it yours to answer. For now a look, a smile, a few words of what you feel, nothing more.
{% elif wed == 6 %}
Now: {{ player.name }} has said yes, and {{ wed_by }} is about to ask you whether you take {{ player.name }}. Wait for the question; it is not your turn yet. No "I do" until {{ wed_by }} has asked you: a look, a smile, nothing more.
{% elif wed == 7 %}
Now: {{ wed_by }} has asked you whether you take {{ player.name }}. Answer as yourself, aloud: yes, if your heart says yes - or, if you cannot, say so, and the wedding stops here.
{% else %}
Now: you have both said yes; {{ wed_by }} is pronouncing you married.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
